# References, definition and rename of a PARAMETER follow its own declaration
# (issues/fixed/2026-10-24-lsp-references-of-a-parameter-match-every-same-named-parameter-of-the-module.md).
# `f` and `g` both declare `x`. A parameter used to bind with the interned
# synthetic token at line 0, column 0, so references on `f`'s `x` also
# returned `g`'s use, definition landed on `f` itself (0:0), and a rename of
# `g`'s `x` rewrote `f`'s body. Now references answer `f`'s declaration and
# use, definition the declaration, and the rename edits `g` only.
timeout=240
framing=strict
